<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy — CaydexWidgets (app extension)

  REQUIRED TO UPLOAD, SEPARATELY FROM THE APP'S. Apple evaluates a required-reason API
  declaration per BINARY, and an app extension is its own binary inside the .ipa. The app
  target's manifest at `ios/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy` does not cover this one; without this file
  the upload can fail ITMS-91053 naming CaydexWidgets specifically, which reads like an app
  problem and is not.

  This became necessary on 2026-09-07. The extension previously "performed no network call and
  held no credential" — it only read the App Group — and even then it used UserDefaults, so
  strictly it always needed a manifest. It now also authenticates a request with a widget token,
  which is why the omission was worth fixing rather than noting.

  Required-reason APIs: UserDefaults only. `UserDefaults(suiteName:)` in `WidgetAPIConfig`,
  `WidgetSnapshotStore` and `MoversConfigurationIntent` — all against the shared App Group
  `group.com.phan.caydex`, hence 1C8F.1 (defaults shared by members of the same App Group).
  ⚠️ This used to declare CA92.1 with the two definitions reversed: CA92.1 is "accessible
  only to the app itself", and this extension never touches its own standard defaults.
  Verified ABSENT from `CaydexWidgets/` and `Shared/`: file-timestamp APIs,
  system boot time, disk space, and active-keyboard APIs.

  Tracking: false. The extension links no SDK at all — its only dependencies are WidgetKit,
  SwiftUI, AppIntents and Foundation.

  NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is EMPTY, and that is a statement, not an oversight. The
  extension makes two requests:
  - one carries the market-scoped widget token and returns a market-wide roll-up;
  - since the Holdings self-refresh (migration 216), one carries the per-device Holdings grant
    key and returns the user's OWN holdings movers.
  The app already collects and declares that data in the app target's manifest. Apple merges
  the declarations across binaries, and restating them here would make the two drift. The
  extension writes only to the shared container (and reads the grant from a ThisDeviceOnly
  Keychain item in the App Group access group). The UserDefaults reason stays 1C8F.1 only:
  `WidgetHoldingsGrant` deliberately uses the App Group, never `.standard`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
	<array/>

	<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
	<array>
		<dict>
			<!-- The App Group suite: the snapshot the app writes, the base-URL override,
			     the market/holdings mode toggle, and the widget token. Reads and writes
			     the shared container only — never the app's own defaults domain. -->
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
			<string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
			<key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
			<array>
				<string>1C8F.1</string>
			</array>
		</dict>
	</array>

	<key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
	<array/>
</dict>
</plist>
